🏠 Rent Now, Pay Later: more flexible apartment rentals in Dubai

One of the key features of Dubai’s rental market is the need to make large upfront payments. While some landlords offer monthly payment options, many still prefer to receive a full year’s rent in advance or split the annual amount into just a few payments.

For tenants, these terms are not always convenient: instead of manageable monthly expenses, they may need to pay a significant amount upfront.

As early as September 2026, Dubai is expected to launch the new Rent Now, Pay Later program, designed to address this issue.

Here’s how the program is expected to work:

🏠the bank pays the landlord the annual rental amount;
🏠the tenant then repays the bank in equal monthly instalments over a period of up to 12 months;
🏠according to preliminary information, the instalment plan is expected to be interest-free.

As a result, the landlord receives the required annual amount, while the tenant can spread the cost over the year — even if the property is initially offered on the condition of full annual payment upfront.

Importantly, the final terms of the program have not yet been confirmed. Details regarding how the program will operate, tenant eligibility requirements, and other conditions are expected to be announced in September.

